First you should ask if each category deserves the same number of slots 
(four).  I suggest that they do not; some are much less interesting or 
competitive than others.  High Score: Role, in particular, shouldn't 
recognize any runners up; either one has it or one doesn't.  Similarly, 
the First Ascension is an achievement, and perhaps the second too, but not 
subsequent ones.  On the other hand, the Fastest Ascension: Gametime, 
Fastest Ascension: Realtime, and Best Behaved Ascension categories are 
skill-testing enough to meaningfully recognize at least the top ten in 
each.

Second place should be worth perhaps 70% of first place.  More than 75% 
doesn't properly reward the distinction between them; less than 60% is too 
top-heavy.   



